💭 A method whose only use of its own object is to return it, called on a fresh object.
💭
💭 Expected: the program prints "404: not here".
💭 What happens: a segmentation fault. MFFunctionAnalyser::recordThis does not count a return as
💭 an escape, so such a method is taken to borrow its object. A fresh object it is called
💭 on is then placed in the caller's frame, and the method's result is that same object:
💭 gone when the caller returns it.
💭
💭 A method that assigns its object first is fine: 👇 ➡️ same, then ↩️ same.
